  "text": "CG\nЦГ\nEN\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAccessibility\nHomepage\nMinistry of Foreign Affairs\nDiplomatic missions\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nPortugal\nPortugal*\nEmbassies and consulates of Montenegro and visa regimes for foreign citizens\nContact\nThe Embassy of Montenegro in French Republic\nVisa regime\nNationals of the Portuguese Republic may enter, cross the territory and stay in Montenegro up to 90 days without visa, with valid travel document.\nNationals of the Portuguese Republic may enter, cross the territory and stay in Montenegro up to 30 days without visa, with valid Identity Card isued by relevant authority of the Hellenic Republic\nDiplomatic Relations\nPortuguese Republic recognized Montenegro's independence on 19th of June 2006, while diplomatic relations were established on 17th of may 2007.\nAmbassador of Montenegro to the Portuguese Republic, based in Paris, is Ivan Ivanišević.\nAmbasador of Portuguese Republic to Montenegro, based in Belgrade, is José Rui Velez Caroço.\nHomepage\nPress room\nAll news\nOrganization\nDocument library\nAsk the Government\nPR contacts\nFacebook\nX\nInstagram\nYouTube\nFlickr\nePayment\neHealth\neGovernment\nеTax\neEnrollment\nCentral Register of Business Entities\nAccessibility\nSite map\nEnglish\n©Copyright 2026. Government of MontenegroOpšti uslovi korišćenjaThis site is protected by reCAPTCHA and applies Googleprivacy policyandterms of serice.",
